          %h2#definition_and_properties Definition and Properties
          %p
            A
            %strong valuation ring
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+domain"} integral domain
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi O
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O
            which satisfies any of the following equivalent conditions:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                for every nonzero element
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                in its
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+of+fractions"} field of fractions
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi O
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in O
                or
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi O
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^{-1} \in O
            %li
              %p
                the ideals of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi O
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O
                are totally ordered by inclusion;
            %li
              %p
                the principal ideals of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi O
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O
                are totally ordered by inclusion.
          %p
            These equivalences are not difficult to establish. For example, if 1. holds and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mo ,
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I, J
            are distinct ideals, then some element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            belongs to one but not the other, say
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in J
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∉
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \notin I
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi I
