              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+order"} linearly ordered
          %h3#example_germs_of_definable_functions Example: germs of definable functions
          %p
            Local rings often arise as stalks of sheaves of real or complex-valued functions, and similarly, some of the more interesting examples of valuation rings arise by considering germs of functions at an “ideal” point, for example at an ultrafilter or infinite point where the functions are not formally defined. Examples such as these are often rich sources of rings and fields with
            = succeed "." do
              %em infinitesimal elements
          %p
            Consider the class of all functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
